,[9.054,11.09,8.92,10.9,3990500],[10.57,11.15,9.84,10.85,2525100],[11.21,11.3,10.35,10.71,1348700],[10.85,10.94,10.18,10.55,861100],[10.35,10.74,10.12,10.56,1001300],[10.51,10.574,9.86,10.225,715600]],"about":{"what":"Funko, Inc. (FNKO). This chart runs from Aug 6, 2020 to Dec 11, 2020.","setup":"The stock rose about 42% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 7 weeks, peaking at $6.72 and pulling back 20% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Oct 23, 2020 it closed at $6.76, its first close above the base high of $6.72. Volume that day was 935K shares, 3.04x the prior 10-day average of 308K. It didn't hold. By Oct 30, 2020 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $10.22.","lesson":"This is an example of a shakeout. The breakout failed by the rules, closing below the level three days running, and then the stock recovered and ran. Cutting it was still the right call when it happened. A failed breakout that fixes itself is worth watching for a re-entry, not a reason to ignore the exit."}}